# Archfiend of Despair: "At the beginning of each end step, each opponent loses life equal to the life that player lost
# this turn." Each Archfiend's ability is its own trigger and reads the opponent's total as it resolves, so a second one
# sees the loss the first caused (2018-06-08 ruling). Bot1 has two Archfiends out by turn 7. On turn 8 Bot2 bolts Bot1
# (20 - 3 = 17) and loses 2 to its own Night's Whisper (20 - 2 = 18); that turn's end step takes 2 and then 4 from Bot2
# (18 - 2 - 4 = 12) and nothing from Bot1, who lost life that turn too but is not an opponent: it stays at 17.

